0..75 Comment "// The simply typed lambda calculus as a theory. A context and a type index"
76..148 Comment "// each of its terms. Its syntax is a first-order model of the signature"
149..215 Comment "// (Kaposi and Xie, _Second-order generalised algebraic theories_,"
216..285 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10). This source is the first rung of"
286..328 Comment "// normalisation by evaluation as a model."
329..331 Comment "//"
332..406 Comment "// The object types, the contexts, the variables and the terms are indexed"
407..482 Comment "// families. A renaming sends each variable of one context to a variable of"
483..558 Comment "// another. The semantic type of an arrow is the Kripke function space over"
559..618 Comment "// renamings. A recursion computes it from the object type."
619..621 Comment "//"
622..698 Comment "// The evaluator, reflection and reification stop at four refusals. The twin"
699..748 Comment "// in the pathological corpus names each of them."
749..751 Comment "//"
752..767 Comment "// - see: #5032"
